        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the infiltration test we notice air leakage from the followings house components:

 - Attic hatch

 - The upper floor windows

 - The back door (around the hitch and the handle)

 - The receptacles

 - The electrical panel

 - Air coming from the header joist on the wall against the location of the oil tank (basement)

 - From the chimney of the furnace

 - The bathroom fan



We recommend to seal the items listed above. All together it contribute to heat loss, an increase of the energy required to heat the living space and it makes the house not comfortable and cold.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>During the assessment the owner mention the idea of insulating the arctic entry. In fact this section even if heated is colder than the rest of the house. We recommend to increse the level of insulation.  You are eligible for a rebate of 2.50$/square foot for the addition of a minimum of R-20.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>After an inspection of the insulation of the attic we found that the level of insulation is not enough and doesn't meet the actual standard. We recommend to increse the level of insulation to reach a level of R-60.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <windows>The window in this house are a double glass units and the upper floor windows are not air tight. We recommend the replacement of the windows for a ENERGY STAR certified windows suitable for ZONE 3.</windows>
                <HeatingSystem>In this moment the house is equipped with an oil furnace heating system. The owner mention the idea of replacing the furnace by a propane furnace.



Propane furnace can be efficent up to 96% and require the installation of propane tank outside. We recommend an electric furnace for the following reasons:

-100%

- No Green Houses Gas

- No pollution

- No risk back draft combustion gases spillage



Perhaps we suggest to fix the air tightness of the house before proceeding to the replacement of the heating system. The simple replacement of the heating unit will not change anything in the house. We recommend to priorise the air sealing of the house before.</HeatingSystem>
                <WaterConservation>In this moment your home is equipped with a 13L toilet. We recommend the replacement of the toilet by a low flow toilet to reduce the water consumption.</WaterConservation>
                <AdditionalComments>During our visit we notice the presence of asbestos material. We recommend to be careful in the management of this type of material. It will be important to monitor regulary the materials containing asbestos. When damaged, some fibres can be released in the interior space and create an exposition to asbestos material.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
